==Russian==
{{wp|ru:}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|ru|pl|muzyka}}. Further from {{der|ru|la|mūsica}}, from {{der|ru|grc|μουσική}}. Also a dated poetic variant ''муз'''ы́'''ка'' is known (via French, now humorous and expressive). {{displaced|ru|sl=1|гудьба́}} (a verbal noun of {{m|ru|гуде́ть}}, akin to {{m|ru|гудо́к}}, {{m|ru|гу́сли}}; compare {{m+|cs|hudba}}, {{m+|pl|gędźba}}).

Note natively formed {{m+|sh|глазба}}, {{m+|sl|glasba}} (i.e. ''гласьба'' (''голосьба''), a verbal noun of {{m|ru|гласи́ть}} ({{m|ru|голоси́ть}}), akin to {{m|ru|глас}} ({{m|ru|го́лос}})).

